From 7c8892edec86db88e98a14ef68cd7d3dffb8e4da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 01:30:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 121/123] dynarmic A64: selects on the host's flags, SXTW
 without a zero-extension first, return stack entries of the PC

A CSEL/CSINC/CSINV/CSNEG/FCSEL whose flags a compare earlier in the block made selects on the
host's flags as that compare of its values sets them right before it (CondFlags* then
ConditionalSelectHost32/64: cmp; cmov) instead of loading the stored flags back; the stored
flags no longer read there can go (GetSetElimination, the dead flags pass). SignExtendWordToLong
of a LeastSignificantWord takes the wide value (movsxd reads the low half). With
return_stack_pc_only the return stack holds return addresses alone and is emptied when the
FPCR's mode bits change: a return compares the PC as it is (8 instructions instead of 14).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01REmpC53sSK3VTcKMxWFSSb
